    "construction_knowledge": "CC0",
    "notes": "Interior species (Zoo 0.84.0). REFERENCE: a Delco bar or diner booth -- dark wood end panels, recessed kick, a vinyl seat on a fascia, a high back of channel-tufted cushions leaning back, a wood cap rail; single, or back to back on one spine when the slot is 1.05 m deep or more -- and a 1990s couch with turned feet, rolled arms, crowned seat and back cushions and a throw pillow. Burgundy, hunter green, teal and mauve are the art direction's accents (docs/DELCO_1997_ART_DIRECTION.md, point 5). Geometry planned purely in core/booth_forms.py. BUILT (0.84.0): booth 740 tris at 1.8 x 0.75 x 1.15, back-to-back 1428 at 2.4 x 1.4 x 1.2 and 2384 at 4.0 x 1.6 x 1.4 (the genome's largest: sixteen channels a side); sofa 650-764. BUDGET 2600: the longest back-to-back booth, measured; a diner row is three or four, a couch is a third of it."
